From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram reads through AND-OR trees without
 tristates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

generate_ram's read path is a tristate bitline per bit, and a library
without a tristate cell (asap7) could not generate at all (RAM-0010).
-read_style and_or reads through a tree per bit column instead: an
AOI22 over each pair of rows, then NAND2 and NOR2 levels by turns, each
node placed in a row of the span it covers, beside its inputs. It is the
default where the library has no tristate cell (RAM-0057 says so), and
can be asked for where it has one; -read_style tristate insists on the
bitlines.

A storage flop whose output is the data inverted is taken on the
AND-OR path, an inverter at the root of each tree undoing it; the
tristate path refuses it (RAM-0058). buildPortMap now reckons a flop's
output polarity from both the state variable a pin reads and its
next_state: asap7's DFFHQNx1 stores !D in IQN and outputs IQN on QN,
which it took for a true output. Cells with next_state "D" are as
before. NAND2 and NOR2 are found by truth table (asap7 writes NAND2 as
(!A) + (!B)), through the evaluator findMaster4 used, now shared.

Tested: src/ram/test/and_or_read_asap7.tcl.

Commit 2 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
